+# GOAL — block 24: unrecorded sites — the free-window reading and the integrated-exterior reading of the static law differ exactly when an unrecorded component touches two recorded sites (2026-09-15)
+
+**Owner directive (2026-09-15):** don't stop; assess the next lane at each conclusion; no subagents; derivations over computation.
+
+**Why this block.** The lane's queue is down to hard or incremental items; the campaign meta note names one seam no block has taken that sits inside this lane: "the claim that unrecorded sites carry no law-level state is a hypothesis for investigation, not an adopted reading". The two readings are exact objects: R1 (free window: the static law of a set of records is normalized over the recorded sites only) and R2 (every site's possibilities enter; records lock, unrecorded sites are summed out). They agree or differ by an exact criterion, with exact witnesses, in the campaign's own currency: a model pair differing on a named target, and the separating clause recorded for the owner.
+
+**Object.** A finite set `W` of recorded sites, a finite set `E` of unrecorded sites adjacent to `W` (the nearest-neighbour graph on `W ∪ E`), the six-axis product rule `φ ∈ {p, q, r}` (same, antipodal, orthogonal; positive) and the sphere rule `e^{βs·s'}`. `μ_W^{R1} ∝ Π_{W-bonds} φ`; `μ_W^{R2}` = the marginal on `W` of `μ_{W∪E} ∝ Π_{all bonds} φ`; `μ_W^{R3}(·|ω)` = the window law with exterior records `ω` (blocks 17, 23).
+
+**Contract.**
+- Q1 (factorization): `μ_W^{R2} ∝ Π_{W-bonds} φ · Π_C F_C(v_{∂C})` over the connected components `C` of `E`, `F_C(v_{∂C}) = Σ_{u ∈ M^C} Π_{C-bonds} φ Π_{W–C bonds} φ`, `∂C` the recorded sites adjacent to `C`; and `μ_W^{R2} = Σ_ω μ_{W∪E}(ω) μ_W^{R3}(·|ω)` (R2 is the R3-average).
+- Q2 (one attachment): `|∂C| = 1 ⇒ F_C` constant, by value-covariance and transitivity of the covariance group on the menu (both menus); hence R1 = R2 whenever every component of `E` touches one recorded site.
+- Q3 (two attachments): for `C = {a}` with `∂C = {x, y}`, `F_C = φ²(v_x, v_y)`, with `φ² = Z₁²P₀ + (p−q)²P_odd + (p+q−2r)²P_even`, constant iff `p = q = r`; for `C` a path of `k` internal bonds between the attachments, `F_C = φ^{k+2}`, constant iff `p = q = r`; in general `F_C` is constant iff both nontrivial isotypic eigenvalues vanish (an exact criterion). Sphere: `F = 4π sinh(β|v_x+v_y|)/(β|v_x+v_y|)`, strictly increasing in `v_x·v_y`.
+- Q4 (witnesses, exact): plaquette plus one exterior site on two adjacent corners: `TV(R1, R2) = 78621/4563820` at `(3,1,2)` (and at `(5,2,4)`, `(2,1,2)`); the cube with the top face unrecorded: `9778807/1312253264` at `(3,1,2)`; two pendant components: `0`.
+- Q5 (the separating clause and the lane): the clause pair recorded, not adopted; every result of the lane on tori is reading-independent; every window result stated uniformly in exterior records (R3) holds under R2 by averaging; R1 results are exactly those stated for free windows.
+- N-gate: the negative "R1 ≠ R2 on the plaquette-plus-site" is exact; escapes: the constant rule; pendant exteriors.
+
+**Lens pass (self-run panel).**
+- *"This is elementary."* Yes; its content is the exact criterion and the campaign-format witness pair on a seam the meta note flags as open.
+- *"Which reading do the axioms take?"* Neither is derived: "Each site has a domain of local possibilities" applies to every site (R2's reading), "Only records are readable" and "A state is a configuration of records" (R1's reading); the block records the clause, adopts nothing.
+- *"Does the lane's earlier work depend on the fork?"* Q5 answers: tori are reading-free; R3-uniform statements cover R2; free-window statements are R1 by declaration.
+
+**Forbidden phrases (beyond the lane's standing list):** "selects the", "the axioms select", "adopt the", "the correct reading", "converge", "certified", "emergent".
+
+**Prior-art search at `origin/main`.** The campaign meta note (the seam); block 01 (the static reading of finite windows); blocks 15–16 (recorded environments); nothing on the fork itself.
